AssistantMessage from Claude: # Grad–Shafranov Equilibrium Model

The name of the PDE is [Grad-Shafranov equation].

the PDE is not time-dependent.

Below, the elliptic (Grad–Shafranov) operator is written as
$\Delta^\* \psi = R\,\partial_R\!\big(\tfrac{1}{R}\partial_R\psi\big) + \partial_{ZZ}\psi = \partial_{RR}\psi - \tfrac{1}{R}\partial_R\psi + \partial_{ZZ}\psi$,
and Solov'ev profiles are used so that $\mu_0\,dp/d\psi = C_1$ (const) and $F\,dF/d\psi = C_2$ (const), giving the explicit source $f(R,Z,\psi)=C_1 R^2 + C_2$ (general nonlinear source $f=\mu_0 R^2 p'(\psi)+F F'(\psi)$ shown for completeness). The weak form is obtained by testing with $v/R$, which makes the operator self-adjoint with weight $1/R$.

