<body>
<h1>Grad&ndash;Shafranov Equilibrium of an Axisymmetric Tokamak</h1>

<p>The name of the PDE is <strong>Grad&ndash;Shafranov equation</strong>.
The PDE is <strong>not time-dependent</strong> (it is an MHD equilibrium equation).</p>

<h2>Grad&ndash;Shafranov operator</h2>
<p>
$$
\Delta^{*}\psi \;\equiv\; R\,\frac{\partial}{\partial R}\!\left(\frac{1}{R}\frac{\partial \psi}{\partial R}\right)
+ \frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial Z^{2}}
\;=\; \frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial R^{2}} - \frac{1}{R}\frac{\partial \psi}{\partial R}
+ \frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial Z^{2}}.
$$
</p>

<h2>Strong form</h2>
<p>Find the poloidal flux \(\psi(R,Z)\) on the cross-section \(\Omega\subset\{R>0\}\) such that</p>
<p>
$$
\Delta^{*}\psi
= -\,\mu_{0}\,R^{2}\,\frac{dp}{d\psi} \;-\; F\,\frac{dF}{d\psi}
\;\equiv\; -\,f(R,Z,\psi)\qquad\text{in }\Omega,
$$
$$
\psi = 0 \qquad\text{on }\partial\Omega .
$$
</p>
<p>With Solov'ev (linear) profiles \( \mu_{0}\,dp/d\psi = C_{1}\), \( F\,dF/d\psi = C_{2}\):</p>
<p>
$$
\frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial R^{2}} - \frac{1}{R}\frac{\partial \psi}{\partial R}
+ \frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial Z^{2}}
= -\left(C_{1}R^{2} + C_{2}\right)\quad\text{in }\Omega,\qquad \psi=0 \text{ on } \partial\Omega .
$$
</p>

<h2>Weak form</h2>
<p>
Multiply by \(v/R\) with \(v\in V_{0}=\{v\in H^{1}(\Omega):v=0\text{ on }\partial\Omega\}\),
integrate over \(\Omega\) with \(dx=dR\,dZ\), and integrate by parts. The weighted
boundary terms vanish since \(v=0\) on \(\partial\Omega\). Find
\(\psi\in H^{1}(\Omega)\), \(\psi=0\) on \(\partial\Omega\), such that for all \(v\in V_{0}\):
</p>
<p>
$$
\int_{\Omega}\frac{1}{R}\,\nabla\psi\cdot\nabla v \; dx
=\int_{\Omega}\frac{1}{R}\,\Big(\mu_{0}R^{2}\,p'(\psi)+F(\psi)F'(\psi)\Big)\,v\;dx .
$$
</p>
<p>Solov'ev specialization (\(f=C_{1}R^{2}+C_{2}\)):</p>
<p>
$$
\int_{\Omega}\frac{1}{R}\,\nabla\psi\cdot\nabla v \; dx
=\int_{\Omega}\Big(C_{1}R+\frac{C_{2}}{R}\Big)\,v\;dx
\qquad\forall v\in V_{0}.
$$
</p>

<h2>Domain (plasma boundary)</h2>
<p>
Rectangular cross-section \(\Omega=[R_{\mathrm{in}},R_{\mathrm{out}}]\times[Z_{\min},Z_{\max}]\),
or a D-shaped boundary (Miller parametrization)
\( R(\theta)=R_{0}+a\cos(\theta+\delta\sin\theta),\; Z(\theta)=\kappa\,a\sin\theta \),
with minor radius \(a\), elongation \(\kappa\), triangularity \(\delta\); \(\psi=0\) on this curve.
</p>
</body>
</html>
